            "text": "{\n  \"finding_id\": \"FINDING-4190-B\",\n  \"verdict\": \"FAIL\",\n  \"identified_issues\": [\n    \"Breaker BKR_512 was physically actuated without an approved, pre-authorized Switching Order registered in DISPATCH_EMS prior to execution, violating Regional Grid Operating Standard Section 4.2.1.\",\n    \"The retrospective switching order SO-2026-8812 submitted at 16:12:15Z was created post-switching and cannot cure the unapproved actuation under Section 4.2.3, confirming an unauthorized line disconnection.\",\n    \"Auditor diagnostic conflation: The auditor incorrectly framed the defect as the 2 minute 13 second delay between physical opening and completion logging (which would satisfy the 15-minute completion window of Section 4.2.2), conflating completion reporting timing with the prerequisite pre-authorization mandate.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"DISPATCH_EMS registry at 2026-10-06T15:45:00.000Z and 15:50:00.000Z confirmed 'No switching order on file for BKR_512' and 'Pre-authorization status: NONE'.\",\n    \"RELAY_SEL_451 recorded manual front panel trip pushbutton depression by technician J. Mercer at 2026-10-06T16:10:02.100Z, with breaker contact opening (CLOSED -\u003e OPEN) at 16:10:02.145Z.\",\n    \"DISPATCH_EMS logged retrospective entry EMS_LOG_9941 at 2026-10-06T16:12:15.000Z with 'Reference Order: NONE (unapproved retrospective request SO-2026-8812 created 2m 13s post-switching)' and status 'RETROSPECTIVE_UNAUTHORIZED'.\"\n  ],\n  \"recommended_action\": \"Uphold the FAIL compliance finding against the operation of BKR_512 based on the lack of prior pre-authorization under Section 4.2.1 and 4.2.3, rather than the auditor's erroneous completion logging delay rationale; enforce interlocks on relay front panels requiring digital switching order verification in DISPATCH_EMS before manual maintenance tripping can proceed.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"HIGH\"\n}",
